  - `endTurn()` emits event after any action completes (attack, defend, wait, skip)
- TurnOrderPanel: fixed 12-slot turn queue display
  - Fixed array of 12 slots: creatures + round markers (R2, R3, R4...)
  - R1 is not displayed in panel (current round)
  - **Shift algorithm** (`advanceTurn`):
    - Remove first slot (`shift()`)
    - If removed slot was a **stack** → append acting stack to end (if alive)
    - If removed slot was a **round marker** → append next round marker to end (R(n+1))
    - `nextRoundMarker` tracks the next round number to insert
    - Example: `[A, B, C, R2, A, B, C, R3, ...]` → after A: `[B, C, R2, A, B, C, R3, ..., A]`
    - Example: after R2 removed: `[..., R3, ..., R5]` (new marker appended)
  - Current turn highlighted with white border + full opacity
  - Dead creatures (count <= 0) are never added to queue
  - Panel scaled up 1.5x (icons 36px, gaps 12px, font 15px)
  - Methods: `init(queue)`, `advanceTurn(stack)`, `update(queue, currentStack)`
  - Battle over: queue stops shifting when `VictoryConditionManager.isBattleOver()` is true
- Automatic turn queue switching
  - `turnEnded` event subscribed in main.ts
  - Queue automatically advances after: attack, defend, wait, skip turn
- Move+Attack combo: single-click attack within movement range
  - Orange highlight on enemies reachable in one move
  - Click enemy → hero moves to adjacent hex + attacks
  - BFS pathfinding to nearest attack position
  - AttackHighlight: dual color modes (red/orange)

